Subject: [PATCH] aji_trt: replace weak basename+CRC32 cache with content-addressed

The original uses basename + crc32(settings) + gpu token. This collides
on different ONNX with same name and deletes foreign files via
clean_stale_engines.

Replace with content-addressed using GraphContentIdentity + EngineBuildIdentity
from manifest (see M14). Use buildKey() for lookup, record engineSha256 after
serialize. Never touch user model dirs.

Also add preparedOnly mode that refuses configure if no pre-built engine.

diff --git a/src/aji_trt.cpp b/src/aji_trt.cpp
index ...
--- a/src/aji_trt.cpp
+++ b/src/aji_trt.cpp
@@
- std::string engine_path_for(...) {
-     return model_dir / (onnx_name + "." + crc32(settings) + suffix);
- }
- void clean_stale_engines(...) { delete foreign .engine; }
+ // Mikai: use manifest-driven content address
+ std::string engine_path_for(const BuildKey& key) {
+     return artifact_dir / key + ".engine";
+ }
+ // no clean_stale that touches outside our root
---
# High-level patch. Owner clarification: MIT, proceed with adoption.
